'''''Muehlenbeckia sagittifolia''''' is a species of flowering plant native to [[South America]] (in northern [[Argentina]], [[Uruguay]], [[Paraguay]], [[Bolivia]] and southern [[Brazil]]). Outside of its range, it has been introduced in [[Portugal]] (including the [[Azores]] and [[Madeira]] archipelagos)<ref>{{cite web |title=Muehlenbeckia sagittifolia (Ortega) Meisn. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:1155902-2 |website=Plants of the World Online |access-date=20 February 2023 |language=en}}</ref>

